ers/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.7.beta5.official [bbd3f43b5]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.beta5 - macOS Sequoia (15.7.3) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M4 Max (Apple9) - Apple M4 Max (16 threads) - 128.0 GiB memory - CoreAudio (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen navigating in the file system popup when choosing to import a project, I was unable to navigate to folders that were behind aliases. It would be useful to navigate through the alias, and then when a file is selected the filesystem would return the true path.\n\nThere also is the issue that file aliases are not respected, but this is less of an issue and would have less edge cases.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a folder (or file), then right click and create an alias of it. Try to import a project from the Godot project manager, and navigate to where the alias is. Notice that Godot's filesystem does not recognize it as a file or as a folder at all.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A, just need MacOS and Godot","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120132/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120132/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}